WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.170
This walkthrough covers the reference lists
used to prepare a certification plan.

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:13.050
In the previous TPMS, they were five
separate screens under GCP, Maintenance.

3
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:19.290
Delegation was the hardest to read:
one long list of several hundred rows,

4
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.570
each pairing a section
root with an FOC code,

5
00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.710
so seeing what one specialist
covered meant remembering the codes.

6
00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:32.290
In the updated application, the five lists
come together under Compliance Setup,

7
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.950
as tabs with their counts.

8
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.850
Search and Add work on the open tab,

9
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:41.310
and the information button explains what
each list is for and where it is used.

10
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:47.470
Finding of Compliance lists each FOC code
with its authority specialist, specialty,

11
00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:50.870
and whether it is offered
by default on every rule.

12
00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.230
Delegation is now called
Specialist Coverage.

13
00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.390
Specialists appear on the left with
the number of rules they cover;

14
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.810
AP-01, for example, covers 147.

15
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.160
Selecting one shows each section
root, with its regulation title,

16
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.110
limitation and active state.

17
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.390
Add opens with that
specialist already chosen.

18
00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:18.490
Disciplines links each DAO specialty
code to its Elisen and TCCA discipline.

19
00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:22.630
Means of Compliance lists the
methods used to show compliance,

20
00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.980
such as design review or flight test.

21
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:31.070
DDS Types holds the detailed design
specification types for Part 23 work,

22
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.570
and each can now carry its own text.

23
00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.120
One page now holds every list
a compliance plan draws on,

24
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.450
with a clear view of which
rules each specialist covers.
